# Third-party benchmark checkout. Carries its own .git and licence, so it is
# a dependency to fetch, not source to vendor. Note that no experiment in this
# repository reads it: the MemoryAgentBench-named scripts never contained a
# path, loader or open() for this directory, and they are untracked below.
experiments/data/MemoryAgentBench/

# Never-run experiment scripts, untracked rather than deleted so the working
# ideas survive on disk. All three were added in 0657956, were never modified,
# and define no results directory at all, so there was nowhere they could ever
# have written output. Each also carries a defect from a family already
# retracted elsewhere in this repository:
#   exp19 - Task 2 adds one memory to a fresh store then asks for k=3, so its
#           criterion cannot fail; Task 4 can pass on a conflict trace whose
#           text still contains the obsolete fact. Its name asserts an
#           evaluation on MemoryAgentBench that the code does not perform.
#   exp20 - configured at threshold 0.70 with requires_marker=False, which is
#           the worst-precision point exp23 characterises (precision 0.367,
#           FPR 0.404), and its pass criterion is defeated by NCM's own
#           conflict-trace text.
#   exp21 - a demo, not an experiment. Its "semantic" encoder returns random
#           vectors, so chain structure is unobservable in principle; recall is
#           trivially 3/3 on a 3-memory store; output is sorted into
#           ground-truth order. scripts/test_multihop_realworld.py, added in
#           the same commit, is the real version.
experiments/python/exp19_memoryagentbench_competencies.py
experiments/python/exp20_memoryagentbench_baseline.py
experiments/python/exp21_multihop_reasoning.py
